Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Geo Backgrounds", "Section",
 CellTags->
  "GeoBackgrounds",ExpressionUUID->"f0189bef-e15b-4be9-9311-90e3c8dabb73"],

Cell["\<\
Typically, one of the aims of geo visualization is to give context to \
locations by placing them on a suitable background. The Wolfram Language \
supports several different background types, supported in all geo \
visualizations. Broadly speaking, these can display maps, satellite imagery \
or elevation information at varying levels of detail, from local street \
features to global topography.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"95bd181b-b712-44db-9546-f6524ce4e2cb"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Maps", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"f8b4f145-62f0-4c04-a1f4-6c8323df0853"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Map backgrounds are automatically rendered at different levels of detail \
depending on the zoom level, which is typically determined by the ",
 ButtonBox["GeoRange",
  BaseStyle->"Hyperlink",
  ButtonData->{
    URL["http://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/GeoRange.html"], None},
  ButtonNote->"http://reference.wolfram.com/language/ref/GeoRange.html"],
 " option."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9104e801-2268-45e6-8fc2-16aa00d173fe"],

Cell["\<\
Plot a smooth histogram of auto theft data in Chicago at two zoom levels:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"878f2e18-7b91-419f-90f2-fabb2ce11e96"],

